tools.description:
Use this when the diver asks how long they can stay at a depth without decompression stops (no-deco limit, NDL, no-stop time). Returns the minutes left after the descent at GF high, the PPO₂ of the gas there and its MOD at 1.4 bar, a safety-stop reminder and a Dive Kit share link. Suits beginners and recreational divers. Not for a full dive plan (plan_dive) or a gas-limited bottom time (find_max_bottom_time).

Computed by the Dive Kit app's Bühlmann ZH-L16C engine; agency tables and dive computers differ. Default gas air, GF 50/80. For "is 25 min at 30 m ok?" send bottom_time_min: the answer says within or over, and by how much. For a repetitive dive pass the previous result's share link and the surface interval.

Example: {"depth":18}

Returns the facts for one breathing gas: maximum operating depth (MOD) at its Dive Kit PPO₂ band cap and at 1.4 bar, minimum depth for hypoxic mixes and, at a depth, PPO₂, equivalent narcotic depth (END), equivalent air depth (EAD) and gas density. Use this when the diver asks whether a gas is OK at a depth, its MOD, END, EAD or density. Not for planning a dive (plan_dive) or picking a gas (best_mix).

Mixes are O₂ % and He %; depth follows units. The band cap is 1.4 bar under 28% O₂, 1.5 to under 45%, 1.6 at 45% and over, unless ppo2_max is given. No engine call.

Example: {"oxygen_pct":32,"depth":35}

Use this when the diver asks what gas to breathe at a depth or which deco gases to carry: returns the richest bottom mix within a PPO₂ limit (default 1.4 bar) and an END limit (default 30 m, 98 ft), the nearest standard fill inside the same limits, and the standard deco gas ladder for that depth with switch depths. Not for checking one named gas (gas_specs) or planning the dive (plan_dive).

The ladder is the common choice, not a prescription: none to 30 m, EANx50 to 45 m, EANx50 and oxygen to 60 m, and a travel gas deeper. A bottom mix under 18% O₂ needs descent_gas in plan_dive. No engine call.

Example: {"depth":50}

Returns scuba cylinders from Dive Kit's vetted open cylinder dataset: water volume, rated capacity, working pressure, material, typical use and, for five or fewer matches, weight, buoyancy and brands. Each row gives the plan_dive cylinder fields (a preset or cylinder_size) that describe it. Use this when a diver asks which cylinder something is, what it holds ("what's an HP100 in litres", "what does an AL80 hold"), or names a cylinder you need to size for plan_dive. Not for gas mixes (gas_specs) or gas used on a dive (plan_dive).

This is Dive Kit's own curated data (MIT licence, open.divekit.app), not a web search. No engine call.

Example: {"query":"hp100","units":"imperial"}

Returns diving certifications from Dive Kit's vetted open dataset of agencies and courses: prerequisites, equivalent courses at other agencies, depth and gas limits, notes and links. Use this when a diver asks what a course allows ("what does PADI Tec 45 let me do"), what they need before a course ("what do I need before a trimix course"), whether two courses are equivalent ("is SSI X equivalent to PADI Y"), or what an agency offers. Not for planning a dive.

This is Dive Kit's own curated data (MIT licence, open.divekit.app), not a web search; agency rules change, so point the diver to the agency for the final word. No engine call.

Example: {"agency":"PADI","query":"tec 45"}

Converts one diving figure between units: pressure (bar, psi, MPa), volume (L, ft³), depth (m, ft), temperature (°C, °F, K), weight (kg, lb) and breathing rate (L/min, ft³/min, bar/min, psi/min). Use this when a diver gives a figure in the other unit system or asks what it reads in another unit. Returns the converted value and the factor used. Not for depth to pressure (gas_specs) or a cylinder's capacity (lookup_cylinders).

quantity names the kind; from and to take unit tokens: bar, psi, mpa; l, cuft; m, ft; c, f, k; kg, lb; l_min, cuft_min, bar_min, psi_min. Converting between a litres rate and bar_min or psi_min needs cylinder_size (water litres of the cylinder, both cylinders for a twinset), because a pressure drop per minute is litres only on one cylinder. Factors are Dive Kit's exact ones (1 bar = 14.5038 psi, 1 ft = 0.3048 m). No engine call.

Example: {"quantity":"pressure","value":3000,"from":"psi","to":"bar"}

Returns the gas one open-circuit cylinder spends over a planned profile: per segment the gas used (volume and pressure), what is left, the runtime and a status, plus the reserve, the turn pressure and the first segment that drops below each. Use this when a diver asks whether a cylinder covers a no-stop or multilevel dive, how much gas a dive uses, or their turn pressure. Not for decompression dives (plan_dive charges deco gas) or measuring a breathing rate (rmv_sac).

sac is the surface breathing rate in L/min (ft³/min imperial), default 20; rmv_sac's rmv and plan_dive's gas_consumption.working_sac are the same figure. Cylinder fields as in plan_dive (preset, cylinder_size, rated_pressure, twinset, start_pressure); default one AL80 at 3000 psi (206.84 bar). reserve as in plan_dive (thirds; fixed defaults to 50 bar, 725 psi). water defaults to en13319; altitude (m or ft) defaults to sea level. Real-gas volumes; the cylinder is assumed to hold air (plan_dive takes any mix). No engine call.

Example: {"preset":"al80","segments":[{"depth":18,"duration_min":40},{"depth":5,"duration_min":3}]}

Returns the mix and pressure a cylinder ends with after gases are added in order: each addition's pressure and mix before and after, the cooling step, and the final O₂ %, He % and pressure. Use this when a diver or blender asks what a fill produced ("50 bar of air, 40 bar of oxygen, then air to 200"), or to check a plan_blend plan: send its mix_result_current as current and its mix_result_additions as additions. Not for planning toward a target (plan_blend) or joining two cylinders with a whip (decant).

Pressures are gauge (bar or psi, per units); mixes are O₂ % and He %. environment sets altitude and the ambient and fill temperatures (defaults sea level, 20 °C, fill equal to ambient); a hot fill settles lower. Real-gas mixing. Analyse the cylinder once it has cooled: the analysed mix, not this one, goes into plan_dive. No engine call.

Example: {"current":{"oxygen_pct":21,"pressure":50},"additions":[{"oxygen_pct":100,"pressure_added":35},{"oxygen_pct":21,"pressure_added":115}]}

Returns a partial-pressure blending plan from what a cylinder holds to a target mix and pressure: bleed, helium, oxygen and top-up steps with the gauge pressure to stop at, the mix after each step, the cooling step, the mix achieved, the gas drawn from each bank and alternative plans. Use this when a diver or blender asks how to fill nitrox or trimix ("fill my twin 12s to 21/35 from 60 bar of 18/45") or whether their banks can reach a mix. Not for a fill already done (mix_result), continuous-flow blending (blend_continuous) or decanting (decant).

current is the cylinder as analysed now: oxygen_pct, helium_pct, pressure, and preset or cylinder_size as in plan_dive (default AL80 size). target: oxygen_pct, helium_pct, pressure. banks default to unlimited air, oxygen and helium; a finite bank needs pressure and cylinder_size together. A target the banks cannot reach returns feasible false with the reason and the partial plan, not an error. To verify, send mix_result_current and mix_result_additions to mix_result; then gas_specs, and plan_dive with the analysed mix. Oxygen above 40% needs oxygen-clean equipment and blender training. No engine call.

Example: {"current":{"oxygen_pct":21,"pressure":50,"preset":"twin_12l"},"target":{"oxygen_pct":21,"helium_pct":35,"pressure":220}}

Returns the settings for continuous-flow blending through a compressor intake: each feed gas's share of the intake flow, the analyzer readings to aim for after the first injection and at the end, and the pressure to bleed to first when the cylinder's gas is in the way. Use this when a blender fills with fixed air, oxygen and helium feeds (a nitrox stick or membrane) and asks what ratios or analyzer targets give a mix. Not for partial-pressure fills (plan_blend).

current is the cylinder now, as in plan_blend; target: oxygen_pct, helium_pct, pressure. injection_order he_first (default) or o2_first picks which intermediate analyzer reading the text leads with; both come back. bleed_step rounds the bleed down to a gauge mark, default 5 bar (100 psi). An impossible mix returns feasible false with the reason. No engine call.

Example: {"current":{"oxygen_pct":21,"pressure":0},"target":{"oxygen_pct":32,"pressure":200}}

Returns what happens when two cylinders are joined with a transfill whip: the pressure both settle to, each cylinder's pressure and mix afterwards, and how much gas moved. With a target mix it also returns where to close the valve, the mix the receiver reaches and what the donor keeps, or why the target is out of reach. Use this when a diver tops up one cylinder from another ("top my 50 bar EANx32 from a full EANx50") or asks whether a decant reaches a mix. Not for bank fills (plan_blend).

receiver and donor as plan_blend's current: oxygen_pct, helium_pct, pressure, and preset or cylinder_size (default AL80 size). Gas flows from the higher pressure to the lower. The warm gas and the whip make the first gauge reading high: analyse after it cools. An unreachable target returns feasible false with the reason. No engine call.

Example: {"receiver":{"oxygen_pct":32,"pressure":50,"cylinder_size":12},"donor":{"oxygen_pct":50,"pressure":200,"cylinder_size":12},"target":{"oxygen_pct":40}}

Returns the gas consumption rate computed from a logged dive's cylinder pressures: RMV (surface litres a minute, what plan_dive and gas_usage take) and SAC (pressure drop a minute on that cylinder), overall and per segment. Use this when a diver gives start and end pressures and asks their SAC, RMV or breathing rate. Give the cylinder's mix for trimix; air is assumed. Not for planning gas (gas_usage, plan_dive).

Each segment is one stretch on one cylinder: depth, duration_min, start_pressure, end_pressure, the cylinder (preset, cylinder_size, rated_pressure, twinset; default AL80) and its mix (oxygen_pct, helium_pct; default air). RMV uses the same real-gas model as the planners: any RMV plans the same dive back to the measured end pressure in plan_dive, and an air RMV does in gas_usage, which assumes air (a trimix RMV reads about 1 to 2 bar optimistic there). SAC is the gauge drop over time and depth. Segments must not overlap in time; the tool cannot check that. sac is null when the segments used different cylinders, and sac_per_cylinder lists each, with the weighted average depth. plan_dive_gas_consumption.working_sac is ready to paste into plan_dive. water defaults to en13319. No engine call.

Example: {"segments":[{"depth":20,"duration_min":20,"start_pressure":200,"end_pressure":140,"preset":"single_12l"}]}

Returns a weighting check for one rig: how much lead to add or remove to be neutral at the end of the dive, the net buoyancy at the start (full cylinders at the target depth) and the end (near-empty cylinders at 3 m), what a flooded drysuit, a failed wing or a dropped stage would do and how to recover, and advisories. Use this when a diver asks how much weight they need, whether a rig is balanced, or how a change of suit, cylinder or water moves it. Not for gas planning.

cylinders take a role (single, twinset, sidemount, stage) and cylinder: a lookup_cylinders id (al80, steel12-232) or a plan_dive preset, or cylinder_size and empty_buoyancy (sea water, with valve), plus empty_weight if known, for one not in the data. Weights are kg (lb imperial); gear weight is positive when it sinks. Omitted fields take Dive Kit defaults (salt water, 30 m, a 5 mm full wetsuit, a 16 kg wing, no body offset), listed in assumptions. Body buoyancy comes only from a measured body_offset (diver), never from body measurements; without one it is taken as neutral. An estimate to start from: confirm with an in-water weight check. Compare two setups with two calls. No engine call.

Example: {"cylinders":[{"role":"single","cylinder":"al80"}],"exposure":{"type":"wetsuit","thickness_mm":7},"gear":[{"label":"belt","weight":6,"ditchable":true}]}
